# Architecture

## Repo layout

```
src/
├── app/                  # Next.js App Router
│   ├── (backend)/        # Server-only routes (API, tRPC endpoints)
│   └── [variants]/       # Client SPA entry points
│       └── (main)/
│           ├── tools/    # Tools Hub (Picbed, future tools)
│           └── ...       # chat, discover, image, settings, etc.
├── features/             # Large self-contained UI feature areas (e.g. Conversation/)
├── store/                # Zustand stores (one per domain)
├── services/             # Client-side service layer (calls tRPC/API)
├── server/
│   ├── routers/          # tRPC routers (see below)
│   └── services/         # Server-side service implementations
├── locales/default/      # i18n source of truth (TypeScript)
└── libs/                 # Shared utilities and abstractions

packages/
├── database/             # Drizzle schemas, models, repositories (@lobechat/database)
├── agent-runtime/        # LLM provider adapters
├── model-bank/           # Model definitions and capabilities
└── ...
```

## Store pattern

Every Zustand store follows this layout:

```
store/<domain>/
├── store.ts          # createWithEqualityFn, merges slices
├── initialState.ts   # Full state type + default values
├── selectors.ts      # Derived state selectors
└── slices/           # Action groups (each slice = one concern)
```

Prefer `vi.spyOn` over `vi.mock` when testing stores.

## Data flow

`Component → useChatStore action → service (src/services/) → tRPC router → server service → DB`

### Chat completion / provider payloads

- **`src/services/chat/index.ts`** assembles **`ChatStreamPayload`** (messages, tools, **`extendParams`** from agent `chatConfig` + model bank `extendParams`).
- **MiniMax:** optional **`trimMinimaxChatContext`** in **`src/services/chat/trimMinimaxContext.ts`** reduces message history when **`messages` + `tools`** would exceed the provider’s effective input budget (see **`provider-model-options.mdc`**).

## tRPC router locations

- `src/server/routers/lambda/` — standard request/response
- `src/server/routers/async/` — long-running / streaming operations
- `src/server/routers/tools/` — agent tool calls

## Path alias

`@/` → `src/`. In tests: `@/database` → `packages/database/src`.

## CSS-in-JS

Use `createStyles` from `antd-style`. Avoid inline styles or plain CSS modules.

## Durable background generation

Leave-topic is not Stop. Graphile Worker owns durable turns; the open tab owns
browser-fallback turns (`unsupported_tool` / `fetch_on_client`). Follow
**`.cursor/rules/durable-background-generation.mdc`** and the OpenWiki lesson
`openwiki/architecture/claude-like-background-generation.md` before changing
send, stop, invalidate, RAG retrieve, or tool continuation.

## Code Interpreter prompts

Builtin `systemRole` stays general sandbox contract. Special tasks go on the
assistant prompt plus sidecar `python-requirements.txt`, not a ChatHub prompt
change. There is no topic system-prompt field. Follow
**`.cursor/rules/code-interpreter-prompt.mdc`**. Jail wrapper / DifySandbox
syscall work must reproduce on a local sidecar image first:
**`.cursor/rules/code-interpreter-sandbox-repro.mdc`**.

## Provider-specific model options

When adding **per-model extension toggles** (gear menu), **extendParams**, or a **new provider option panel**, follow the docs-first workflow in **`provider-model-options.mdc`** (same `.cursor/rules/` folder): official API → model bank → types → service → runtime → UI → i18n → tests.
